     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n**Problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of severe GI intolerance and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, split as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nTell me which of these you want, or give me a different dose. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note that you verified the dose."
      }
     ],
